{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Serve</b> — the opposite of their words: 'we will cast off' — and service of HaShem is fear of Him, and they shall not transgress His mouth." "<b>And rejoice</b> — if rejoicing comes, do not forget that you tremble with fear of HaShem." "And some say: <b>and rejoice</b> — like 'you shall rejoice,' by way of: 'go up and die on the mountain' (Deuteronomy 32:50), 'be fruitful and multiply' (Genesis 1:22), which is a blessing over the fish of the sea. And the meaning: that you shall rejoice if you trembled from HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:05.293370367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}